Description:
≥1: Number of large islands (> 1 km²) from the Global Islands Database (GID) within the shelf;
0: No large islands. Only small islands (< 1 km²) recorded in the GID;
NA: Islands indicated in the topography but absent from the GID

Quality flags: NoGIDMatch (insular due to positive topography but no correspondence to GID);
NoGEBCOLand (insular due to correspondence to GID but no positive topography);
NoShelfArea (no grid cells between 0 and -200 m in the bathymetric raster);
DeepMargin=X (X represents the proportion of polygon area extending beyond the -200 m isobath due to mismatches between topography-derived shelf and island boundaries)
